+// ---- bench instrumentation (scripts/bench/patches/censor-count.patch, not in the apps) -----------------
+// For every objective evaluation: would a lower bound of chi2 have shown, before all finite-source points
+// were computed, that Nelder-Mead rejects the value (see simplex.h's KampylosEvalKind)? The bound is the
+// least-squares chi2 over a subset of the points with its own best (fs, fb): never above the chi2 of all of
+// them. Two orders: time order (what the objective computes today) and cheap first (all point-source points,
+// then the finite-source points in time order, which is what a GPU app's completion step sees). Cost: the
+// contour samples VBMicrolensing reports (NPS, 1 for a point-source point) and the measured time per point.
+// Printed to stderr at exit.
+struct KampylosCensorStats {
